// Rental income and the sale of a rental, for the year that just ended. The shipped
// `us` counts wages, interest, dividends and gains; it has no Schedule E.
//
// Simplifications, on purpose: cash method; the 25,000 USD passive-loss allowance
// is applied without its phase-out above 100,000 USD of income (this person is
// below it); depreciation recapture is taxed as ordinary income, which is right
// while the bracket is below 25%; no state tax.

/// Schedule E: rents received less everything under expenses/rental. A loss
/// offsets other income up to 25,000 USD (IRC §469(i)), and the loss on paper,
/// because of depreciation and interest, is common in the first year.
law schedule-e
  each year
  let net = tally(rental-income) - tally(rental-expenses)
  count net as rental-net
  count max(net, empty - passive-allowance[year]) as agi

/// Rents, late fees and kept deposits count when they arrive (cash method).
law count-rental-income
  on in
  when from is rent-income
  count amount as rental-income

// The passive-loss allowance for active participation in a rental (IRC §469(i)).
param passive-allowance
  2024 25_000 USD
  2025 25_000 USD
  2026 25_000 USD
